@startuml snapshot-capture-sequence
' ============================================================================
' Consumer-driven snapshot capture and graph/callback walk.
' Source of truth: src/bindings.rs (dictionary_snapshot, TraversalSnapshot,
' dictionary_edges) + src/ffi.rs (ldict_dictionary_resource); verified live by
' the compile-and-run example in docs/bindings/c-abi-reference.md.
' Color key (family palette + ABI concept colors):
'   #FADBD8 foreign consumer (e.g. liblevenshtein)
'   #D5F5E3 libdictenstein producer surfaces
'   #DCEDC8 VtResource handle / ResourceContext
'   #FFECB3 immutable graph or leased fallback arena (TraversalSnapshot)
'   #FFCDD2 + #B71C1C trust boundary between the two binaries
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 150
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #B71C1C
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFEBEE
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam participantBorderColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #FFCDD2
skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #B71C1C

title Snapshot capture and walk — retain → query_interface → snapshot →\n<latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> revision capture → graph fast path or lazy fallback → release chain

participant "Consumer\n(foreign binary,\ne.g. liblevenshtein)" as C #FADBD8
participant "ldict_* C ABI\n(src/ffi.rs)" as F #D5F5E3
participant "ResourceContext\n(payload: Live)" as R #DCEDC8
participant "Backend revision\n(e.g. DynamicDAWG)" as B #D5F5E3
participant "TraversalSnapshot\n(graph once-cells +\nchunked fallback arena)" as S #FFECB3

== every call below crosses the trust boundary: two independently compiled binaries ==

C -> F : ldict_dictionary_resource(dict, &res)
activate F
F --> C : res = { context, vtable } — **borrowed** two words
deactivate F
note right of C #FFEBEE
  **Copy-not-retain law**: copying the two words
  confers no ownership. A consumer that stores
  them must retain first.
end note
C -> R : res.vtable->retain(res.context)
note right of R : Arc strong count += 1\n(one owned retain per stored copy)

C -> R : query_interface("vt.dictionary.v1",\nminimum_version = 1, &vt)
R --> C : 'static VtDictionaryVTable\n(unit_domain, flags = PARALLEL_REENTRANT)

C -> R : vt->snapshot(res.context, &snap)
activate R
R -> B : backend.root()
activate B
B --> R : root handle of the **published revision**
deactivate B
note right of R #FFECB3
  <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> capture: the revision is immutable and
  structurally shared — no traversal, no copy
  (Driscoll et al. 1989). Graph projection is
  deferred; the fallback arena starts at root.
end note
R -> S : TraversalSnapshot::new(root)
R --> C : snap — **born with one retain**\n(mem::forget transfers it to the consumer)
deactivate R

C -> F : ldict_dictionary_remove_text(dict, "cot")
F -> B : publish successor revision
note right of B : Mutations after capture are\ninvisible to the pinned revision.

== immutable traversal — negotiate the compact graph first ==

C -> S : query_interface("vt.dict.graph.v1", 1, &graph_vt)
alt DynamicDAWG snapshot supports compact graph
  S --> C : graph_vt = 'static VtDictionaryGraphVTable
  C -> S : graph_vt->graph(&view)
  activate S
  S -> S : first call: project retained root and\npublish native + ABI flat arrays\noutside backend/memo locks
  S --> C : stable nodes, edges, root, counts
  deactivate S
  C -> S : graph_vt->node_value_u64(checked dense cursor)
else backend has no compact projection
  S --> C : Unsupported
  C -> S : vt.dictionary root() → leased root id
  loop until start ≥ out_total
    C -> S : node_edges(node, start, out_edges,\ncapacity, &written, &total)
    activate S
    S -> S : ensure_edges(node): enumerate once,\nreserve atomic id range, publish\nwrite-once slots; lock only if a\nnew directory chunk is required
    S --> C : one page: written ≤ capacity,\ntotal stable across pages
    deactivate S
  end
end
note right of C
  Paging law: pages concatenate losslessly;
  <latex>\mathrm{written} = \min(\mathrm{capacity},\ \mathrm{total} - \mathrm{start})</latex>
end note
C -> S : fallback only: node_is_final(id) ·\nnode_value_u64(id) · node_transition(id, label)

== teardown — one release per owned retain; any order ==

C -> S : snap.vtable->release(snap.context)
note right of S : strong count 1 → 0:\ngraph/fallback storage and\npinned revision freed
C -> R : res.vtable->release(res.context)
note right of R : handle keeps its own retain —\nthe dictionary stays alive until\nldict_dictionary_free
C -> F : ldict_dictionary_free(dict)
@enduml
